issue_comments.body:
@hiyouga Could you help confirm the approach and route this PT data-collation fix to the appropriate reviewer? When LlamaFactory falls back to PAD=EOS, the current collator silently removes real EOS labels, including boundaries inside packed documents. This change uses the attention mask to distinguish padding from real EOS tokens.

The description includes the recorded before/after tests on Transformers 4.55.0 and 5.8.0 and a Qwen3-0.6B RTX 5090 smoke test: real EOS supervision changes from 0/6 to 6/6 while all padding positions remain ignored. Both PT entry points select the tested collator; HyperParallel distributed execution has not been validated locally. I would especially appreciate feedback on whether this shared collator is the preferred integration point for those two workflows.

The four workflows on current head `840ce9a` still require approval. Could you authorize them so upstream validation can proceed? Thank you.
